course: dictionary
lesson: 13038
title: Fancier: more decorated, or a hobby keeper
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Fancy is the base word. Fancier is the comparison form, like tall, taller and tallest. When one thing has more decoration or style than another, it is fancier. «The café on the corner is fancier than the one by the station.» The clue is the word than: it compares two places, so fancier means more posh or decorated.
explain: Fancier can also be a noun, meaning a person. A fancier keeps or breeds a certain animal or plant as a hobby. «Mr Patel is a pigeon fancier, and he keeps forty birds in his garden shed.» The words pigeon fancier tell you what he keeps. Ask yourself: what is this person fond of?
explain: Use the swap test to check. In «The fancier hat is bright red with a silver band», swap in more decorated and the sentence still works. So fancier here is an adjective. In «The rose fancier showed her prize flowers», swap in a person who keeps roses as a hobby and it still makes sense.
fact: Fancy is the base word, fancier is the comparison, and fanciest is the top of the scale.
fact: «Fancier» (adjective) means more decorated, elaborate or posh than something else.
fact: «A fancier» (noun) is a person who keeps or breeds a certain kind of animal or plant as a hobby.
fact: Phrases to know: fancier than, pigeon fancier, rose fancier.
fact: The hobby meaning is common in UK and older writing, such as pigeon fanciers in the north of England.
exercise: «The new bakery is fancier than the old one, with gold lettering and glass cake stands.» What does fancier mean here? | *More decorated and posh | Older and wetter | More dangerous | Smaller and quieter
exercise: Mrs Lee is a rose fancier. What is she? | A rose that is very tall | A kind of red flower | Someone who sells roses in a shop | *Someone who keeps roses as a hobby
exercise: Find and copy the comparison form of fancy in «The fancier cars were parked at the front.» | parked | front | *fancier | cars
test: «Tom's sandwich looked fancier once Dad added cress and a curl of cheese.» What does fancier mean here? | *More decorated and posh | Hungrier | Sadder
test: Which sentence uses fancier as a noun, meaning a hobby keeper? | The fancier hat sat on her head | *The fancier showed his birds at the county show | Her cake looked fancier than mine
exam: Which word is the comparison form used to compare two things? | fanciest | fancily | fancy | *fancier
